  "id": "COMPOUND:22242 - PROTEIN:4978",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Commersonine may be involved in the regulation of C8166 through multiple distinct biological pathways. Pathway 1 links Commersonine to Aconitate hydratase, a mitochondrial enzyme, which is targeted by Cauloside B, and ultimately targets C8166. Pathway 2 and 3 indicate that Commersonine also interacts with the DNMT3A2/3L complex, which is targeted by (R)-(-)-2-Amino-1-propanol and Suksdorfin, both of which also target C8166. These findings suggest that Commersonine may act through different mechanisms to influence C8166, potentially through enzyme inhibition or regulatory interactions. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the relationship, with Commersonine possibly modulating C8166 via multiple molecular targets. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Commersonine and C8166, though the exact nature of the interactions remains to be fully elucidated.",
